%T A401523 0,1,1,6,8,0,1,3,0,0,9,4,8,8,1,4,2,3,5,6,5,7,9,8,4,8,0,4,7,0,6,4,6,6,
%U A401523 3,2,9,9,3,9,8,5,9,0,1,3,1,1,8,0,3,5,7,5
%N A401523 The first positive real value of sqrt(j^2 + k^2 - 2*j*k*cos(j-k)) - sqrt(2*k*(k+1)*(1-cos(1)) + 1) - sqrt(2*j*(j+1)*(1-cos(1)) + 1), where j, k are nonnegative integers with k as small as possible and j < k.
%C A401523 The first positive value when k is as small as possible is for k = 15 and j = 12, giving the value sqrt(9 + 360*(1 - cos(3))) - sqrt(480*(1 - cos(1)) + 1) - sqrt(312*(1 - cos(1)) + 1).
%C A401523 This value corresponds to the distance between the circumferences of the 16th and 13th circles in A401497, as sqrt(j^2 + k^2 - 2*j*k*cos(j-k)) is the distance between the centers of any two circles at angles j and k, while sqrt(2*k*(k+1)*(1-cos(1)) + 1) is the radius of the (k-1)-th circle.
%C A401523 The author thanks _Michael De Vlieger_ for confirmation of the minimum positive value.
%F A401523 Equals sqrt(9 + 360*(1 - cos(3))) - sqrt(480*(1 - cos(1)) + 1) - sqrt(312*(1 - cos(1)) + 1).
%e A401523 0.0273981814938231660745532669008394011680130094881423565798480... .
%t A401523 N[ sqrt(9 + 360*(1 - cos(3))) - sqrt(480*(1 - cos(1)) + 1) - sqrt(312*(1 - cos(1)) + 1) , 200 ]
